! ansys_apdl_template.mac
!
! SUPERSEDED for now by the native ANSYS Mechanical (Workbench) workflow in
! ANSYS_MECHANICAL_WORKFLOW.md -- that workflow meshes and solves directly
! in Mechanical, since HyperMesh Student Edition can only export to
! OptiStruct/RADIOSS (.fem), not the ANSYS .cdb format this macro expects.
!
! Kept here as a documented next-level-automation path: once you have a
! working Mechanical-based solve, this is what a scripted, command-line
! batch version of the same solve would look like if you later get access
! to a HyperMesh license that can export ANSYS .cdb, or generate one via
! Mechanical's own "Write Input File" or APDL Command Snippet export.
!
! Static structural solve of the meshed bracket (from mesh_scripts/) under
! the peak suspension-mount load derived from the quarter-car dynamics
! model (dynamics_matlab/). Extracts max von Mises stress and part mass.
!
! Usage: run in batch mode, e.g.
!   ansys232 -b -i ansys_apdl_template.mac -o run.out -p_mesh <mesh.cdb> -p_load <peak_force_N>

/CLEAR
/FILNAME,bracket_static,1
/PREP7

! --- 1. Import mesh exported from HyperMesh ---
CDREAD,DB,%p_mesh%,CDB

! --- 2. Material (placeholder: generic structural steel) ---
! TODO: replace with the actual candidate material's properties
MP,EX,1,210E9      ! Young's modulus [Pa]
MP,PRXY,1,0.3       ! Poisson's ratio
MP,DENS,1,7850      ! density [kg/m^3], needed for mass output

! --- 3. Boundary conditions ---
! TODO: apply fixed constraints at the bracket's chassis-side mounting
! holes (named selection from HyperMesh, e.g. "FIXED_HOLES")
CMSEL,S,FIXED_HOLES
D,ALL,ALL,0
ALLSEL

! --- 4. Apply peak load at the suspension-side mount ---
! %p_load% passed in from the Python orchestration script, sourced from
! quarter_car_ode.m / the Simulink model's peak_force output
CMSEL,S,LOAD_NODE
F,ALL,FY,-%p_load%
ALLSEL

FINISH
/SOLU
ANTYPE,STATIC
SOLVE
FINISH

/POST1
! --- 5. Extract results for the automation pipeline ---
*GET,MAX_STRESS,NODE,0,S,EQV,MAX
*GET,TOTAL_MASS,ELEM,0,MTOT,X   ! total mass from element summary

*CFOPEN,results_summary,csv,,APPEND
*VWRITE,MAX_STRESS,TOTAL_MASS
(F12.2,',',F12.4)
*CFCLOSE

FINISH
